zymogen	n:any of a group of compounds that are inactive precursors of enzymes and require some change (such as the hydrolysis of a fragment that masks an active enzyme) to become active
zymoid	a:resembling an enzyme
zymology	n:the branch of chemistry concerned with fermentation (as in making wine or brewing or distilling)
zymolysis	n:a process in which an agent causes an organic substance to break down into simpler substances; especially, the anaerobic breakdown of sugar into alcohol
zymolytic	a:of or relating to or causing fermentation
zymosis	n:a process in which an agent causes an organic substance to break down into simpler substances; especially, the anaerobic breakdown of sugar into alcoholn:(medicine) the development and spread of an infectious disease (especially one caused by a fungus)
zymotic	a:of or relating to or causing fermentationa:relating to or caused by infection
zymurgy	n:the branch of chemistry concerned with fermentation (as in making wine or brewing or distilling)
zyrian	n:the Finnic language spoken by the Komi
